#====================================================================
# Draft knowledge entry - eigen unsupported ThreadPool pthread_cancel boundary
# Source package: eigen/3.4.1
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-eigen-3.4.1-unsupported-threadpool-pthread-cancel-boundary
trigger_tool:           prescan|clang|conan|shadow-ci
phase:                  preflight|scope-definition|testing
error_signature:        unsupported/Eigen/CXX11/src/ThreadPool/ThreadCancel.h|pthread_cancel|EIGEN_THREAD_CANCEL|EIGEN_OS_GNULINUX

severity:               2
category:               eigen|pthread|unsupported-api|test-scope
match_keywords:         eigen, unsupported, ThreadPool, Tensor, pthread_cancel, EIGEN_OS_GNULINUX, Dense smoke test, OHOS
title:                  Eigen Dense validation does not prove unsupported ThreadPool pthread_cancel behavior

root_cause:             Eigen ships unsupported ThreadPool headers that mention pthread_cancel behind
                        an EIGEN_OS_GNULINUX guard. The package installs unsupported/ but the current
                        consumer test exercises only Eigen/Dense, so ThreadPool behavior remains outside
                        the validated surface.
affected_scope:         Downstream packages that include Eigen unsupported CXX11 ThreadPool or Tensor
                        headers on OHOS, especially if they rely on thread cancellation semantics.
verification_cmd:       python scripts/ohc-run.py prescan --no-writeback --json <extracted-eigen-source>

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           mark-unsupported-threadpool-boundary
rec_description:        Record pthread_cancel as a pre-scan risk without patching core Eigen. For
                        downstream ThreadPool/Tensor users, add a targeted compile and runtime probe
                        before claiming support.
rec_command:            grep -R -n "pthread_cancel\\|EIGEN_THREAD_CANCEL\\|EIGEN_OS_GNULINUX" unsupported/Eigen/CXX11/src/ThreadPool
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               manual

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      narrow-feature-guard
fallback_description:   If OHOS ever enters the GNU/Linux cancellation branch, guard the cancellation
                        macro by a real pthread_cancel feature check or an OHOS-specific exclusion.
fallback_command:       grep -R -n "unsupported/Eigen/CXX11/ThreadPool\\|unsupported/Eigen/CXX11/Tensor" <downstream-source>
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          source-patch

forbid_1_pattern:       Dense.*proves.*ThreadPool|unsupported.*validated.*matmul
forbid_1_reason:        A Dense matrix smoke test does not instantiate or execute unsupported ThreadPool code.
forbid_1_consequence:   Downstream Tensor/ThreadPool users may hit pthread cancellation gaps after the base package is marked done.

similar_to:             [E085,E127,E320]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

doc_file:               knowledge/drafts/DRAFT-eigen-3.4.1-unsupported-threadpool-pthread-cancel-boundary.md
last_updated:           2026-08-28
source_event:           eigen/3.4.1 pre-scan and shadow CI r2 Dense-only validation

